{"lines":[{"t":"Reading","x":0.78752251502218618,"y":0.03757249744588631,"c":1,"w":0.0809700075785319,"h":0.016424772283452183},{"w":0.78213048299153642,"t":"Researchers like Colton don't believe it is right to measure machine creativity directly","x":0.052560365959022116,"y":0.083571927107577659,"h":0.022878280855806343,"c":1},{"w":0.77658294677734374,"h":0.025535035732094924,"y":0.10171988543886956,"c":1,"x":0.050638274853208716,"t":"to that of humans who 'have had millennia to develop our skills'. Others, though, are"},{"y":0.12274408274613979,"c":1,"t":"fascinated by the prospect that a computer might create something as original and","x":0.052560651216571636,"w":0.75952758789062502,"h":0.021605718235622517},{"c":1,"x":0.054457811518904484,"w":0.75575302124023436,"t":"subtle as our best artists. So far, only one has come close. Composer David Cope","h":0.021652671190054318,"y":0.14175129659226615},{"h":0.021812989185183373,"x":0.052568535626677244,"c":1,"y":0.16058343973946165,"w":0.76704355875651031,"t":"invented a program called Experiments in Musical Intelligence, or EMI. Not only did"},{"c":1,"y":0.17921103023600771,"t":"EMI create compositions in Cope's style, but also that of the most revered classical","h":0.021199957754868382,"w":0.76702901204427087,"x":0.054462579308113657},{"y":0.19896973581151356,"t":"composers, including Bach, Chopin and Mozart. Audiences were moved to tears, and","x":0.054511273086851213,"c":1,"h":0.019053519961915288,"w":0.78759399414062503},{"h":0.021911967437802993,"x":0.056330048432653823,"y":0.21722340131059337,"t":"EMI even fooled classical music experts into thinking they were hearing genuine Bach.","c":1,"w":0.79900100708007815},{"t":"Not everyone was impressed however. Some, such as Wiggins, have blasted Cope's","c":1,"h":0.020385560418280657,"x":0.056327148473449141,"y":0.23687265213626629,"w":0.78207636515299483},{"w":0.79338862101236973,"t":"work as pseudoscience, and condemned him for his deliberately vague explanation of","c":1,"y":0.25578810835267074,"x":0.056313806911641201,"h":0.02065915134132712},{"y":0.27466309629627361,"x":0.056313929859036209,"w":0.77083297729492195,"c":1,"h":0.02092402716720787,"t":"how the software worked. Meanwhile, Douglas Hofstadter of Indiana University said"},{"y":0.29313176415819142,"h":0.022120567267737812,"c":1,"t":"EMI created replicas which still rely completely on the original artist's creative impulses.","x":0.058139630870722193,"w":0.80661015828450522},{"h":0.022962234899910117,"c":1,"t":"When audiences found out the truth they were often outraged with Cope, and one music","x":0.056273763166484705,"y":0.31239664361881458,"w":0.81789983113606768},{"c":1,"x":0.054435313934865517,"t":"lover even tried to punch him. Amid such controversy, Cope destroyed EMl's","w":0.71067214965820313,"h":0.021678231872440668,"y":0.33157571317863155},{"c":1,"t":"vital databases.","h":0.016097875080489321,"w":0.14661654154459636,"x":0.058270676465113525,"y":0.35608499707038332},{"h":0.025275810718229375,"c":1,"t":"But why did so many people love the music, yet recoil when they discovered how it","x":0.058077145173174451,"y":0.38666709821229572,"w":0.76733337402343749},{"x":0.058109336563440098,"y":0.40772881592035359,"w":0.77287373860677089,"h":0.022729050783057758,"c":1,"t":"was composed? A study by computer scientist David Moffat of Glasgow Caledonian"},{"y":0.42527408338956929,"x":0.059919491117241722,"t":"University provides a clue. He asked both expert musicians and non-experts to assess","w":0.79743784586588529,"h":0.024828179452162868,"c":1},{"x":0.059935101220923076,"y":0.44583168571286869,"w":0.76168757120768227,"t":"six compositions. The participants weren't told beforehand whether the tunes were","h":0.023899611395094666,"c":1},{"h":0.027006796537793476,"t":"composed by humans or computers, but were asked to guess, and then rate how much","y":0.46352484488846113,"c":1,"x":0.059913294582638346,"w":0.80692621866861969},{"x":0.05986088488549058,"y":0.48171123641008595,"t":"they liked each one. People who thought the composer was a computer tended to dislike","w":0.82012044270833329,"c":1,"h":0.027497976269940105},{"t":"the piece more than those who believed it was human. This was true even among the","y":0.50096085554342806,"w":0.79193283081054688,"h":0.027232852353638259,"x":0.059861508843179458,"c":1},{"h":0.031455256750103078,"c":1,"x":0.061647825855699716,"y":0.51921298119109349,"t":"experts, who might have been expected to be more objective in their analyses.","w":0.7299695332845052},{"w":0.81269556681315114,"x":0.061747801053301431,"h":0.030574462065294461,"t":"Where does this prejudice come from? Paul Bloom of Yale University has a suggestion:","c":1,"y":0.55655000880675909},{"c":1,"t":"he reckons part of the pleasure we get from art stems from the creative process behind","y":0.57605439252066726,"x":0.061763555557567622,"w":0.80702601114908856,"h":0.030557751578818015},{"w":0.8128371175130209,"x":0.061624679254364122,"t":"the work. This can give it an 'irresistible essence', says Bloom. Meanwhile, experiments","y":0.59260643503139832,"h":0.034134738919662788,"c":1},{"c":1,"h":0.033772133890460299,"t":"by Justin Kruger of New York University have shown that people's enjoyment of an","x":0.063479713748876634,"y":0.61293453365020434,"w":0.76400060017903648},{"w":0.78641082763671877,"t":"artwork increases if they think more time and effort was needed to create it. Similarly,","y":0.63291404825694053,"h":0.032476428855409689,"c":1,"x":0.063522886708321943},{"x":0.063608126166144724,"w":0.79582799275716143,"t":"Colton thinks that when people experience art, they wonder what the artist might have","y":0.65162310190839534,"c":1,"h":0.033374949723616543},{"x":0.065411025351394494,"w":0.78290959676106764,"y":0.67085468602518072,"t":"been thinking or what the artist is trying to tell them. It seems obvious, therefore, that","h":0.033564334827626885,"c":1},{"c":1,"h":0.036185650846993545,"y":0.68800414722143977,"t":"with computers producing art, this speculation is cut short - there's nothing to explore.","x":0.063486488866820512,"w":0.79960286458333341},{"x":0.065465429380484469,"y":0.70990904688656287,"w":0.75078287760416662,"t":"But as technology becomes increasingly complex, finding those greater depths in","h":0.032678079697215257,"c":1},{"y":0.72748229050772173,"c":1,"w":0.77149754842122387,"x":0.065430011878379546,"h":0.03466114135074061,"t":"computer art could become possible. This is precisely why Colton asks the Painting"},{"w":0.80729939778645843,"t":"Fool to tap into online social networks for its inspiration: hopetully this way it will choose","y":0.74641065453975042,"x":0.067255792940743783,"h":0.034468946192852568,"c":1},{"c":1,"x":0.065451898582324572,"w":0.41983385721842448,"h":0.025633114963981019,"t":"themes that will already be meaningful to us.","y":0.77472929406855995},{"w":0.028195489247640038,"y":0.95930232527844728,"x":0.86466165389121763,"c":1,"h":0.017441860722175129,"t":"25"}],"h":3106,"w":2400}